A||||2||JohnnyK||High oil pressure||||1||
Z||000000||JohnnyK||08-15-2000||05:20 PM||||I'm not sure where it is supposed to be, but my oil pressure guage reads around the 1/2 to 3/4 lines, but usually at the 3/4 line. What causes this, and is it harmful?||||reg||1
Z||000001||StuGood||08-16-2000||01:09 AM||||It all sounds okay to me.  By the way, generally speaking, oil pressure increases with engine RPMs, and  decreases as the engine warms up and the oil thins out.  So if the oil pressure reads high right after you start the cold engine in the morning, but shows a lower reading at the next stoplight on the way to work, that's normal  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.<P>I wouldn't be too concerned unless the oil pressure reading is consistently low - or, if the idiot light comes on.  Could mean you're low on oil, or oil pump /pressure regulator failing, or worse, bearing clearances opening up due to wear  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">.         ||||reg||14
Z||000002||rogergarrison||08-16-2000||06:03 PM||||my 86 with a 3.1, pretty well modified with a turbo and plenty of other goodies runs about 75 pnd above idle. 50 when its hot in traffic stops. I use Castrol Synthetic. btw I had a Jag XJS i drove for 4 years and 78K with under 10 pnds and 4 or 5 at idle.(of course could have had bad gage i guess, but it did tick a lot).||||reg||1
